exports[`toMarkdown on the food-delivery fixture > matches the snapshot 1`] = `
"# Project plan

> An online food delivery app where customers order from nearby restaurants, pay online and follow the courier live, while restaurants run their menus and orders and couriers deliver.

## Overview

An online food delivery platform for one city: customers browse, order, pay and track, restaurants run menus and orders, and couriers deliver. 13 requirements become 4 epics, 10 stories and 27 tasks (117 points) over 4 sprints.

| Measure | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Requirements | 13 (10 functional, 3 non-functional) |
| Epics / stories / tasks | 4 / 10 / 27 |
| Total estimate | 117 points, 468 hours |
| Sprint plan | 4 sprints, 40 days (capacity 40 points and 60 h per sprint) |
| Shortest possible duration (CPM, unlimited people) | 172 h, 28.5 working days |
| Critical tasks | 9 of 27 |
| Risks | 5 (3 high, 2 medium, 0 low) |
| Issues | 3 |

Configuration: 4 people, 10 points per person per sprint, 10-day sprints, 6 focus hours per day, relaxed sprint packing. Plan schema 1.0.

## Assumptions

- Single-city launch with about 200 restaurants and 50 couriers.
- Card and wallet payments go through a hosted payment provider; the platform never stores card numbers.
- Couriers use a mobile web app in v1; there are no native iOS or Android apps.
- Restaurants are onboarded by operations staff; there is no self-service restaurant sign-up in v1.
- Delivery fees are flat per restaurant; promotions, coupons and surge pricing are out of scope.
- One language (English) and one currency.
- The team is four full-stack developers working in 10-day sprints.

## Requirements traceability

12 of 13 requirements have a story and 12 have a task. Uncovered: R-010.

| Requirement | Type | Priority | Text | Stories | Tasks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| R-001 | functional | must | Customers can find restaurants near their location and browse menus, filtering by cuisine and searching by name or dish. | S-001 | T-001, T-002, T-003, T-004 |
| R-002 | functional | must | Customers can add dishes to a cart and place an order for a chosen delivery address, with optional notes for the restaurant. | S-002 | T-005, T-006, T-007 |
| R-003 | functional | must | Customers, restaurant staff and couriers can register and sign in; customers keep saved addresses and their order history. | S-003, S-007 | T-008, T-009, T-010, T-018 |
| R-004 | functional | must | Customers can pay online by card or digital wallet; an order reaches the restaurant only after the payment is confirmed. | S-004 | T-011, T-012, T-013 |
| R-005 | functional | must | Customers can follow an order from accepted to delivered and see the courier's position on a map while it is on the way. | S-005 | T-014, T-015, T-016 |
| R-006 | functional | should | Customers receive a push, SMS or email notification when the order status changes. | S-006 | T-017 |
| R-007 | functional | must | Restaurant staff can edit menu items, prices and availability, and changes appear to customers within one minute. | S-007 | T-018, T-019 |
| R-008 | functional | must | Restaurant staff see new orders as they arrive and can accept or reject each one, stating a preparation time. | S-008 | T-020 |
| R-009 | functional | must | Couriers receive delivery offers, accept one, and update its status from pickup to hand-over. | S-009 | T-021, T-022 |
| R-010 | functional | could | Customers can rate the restaurant and the courier after delivery and leave a short review. | - | UNCOVERED |
| R-011 | non_functional (performance) | must | Restaurant search and menu pages respond in under 2 seconds at the 95th percentile on a 4G connection, with 5,000 restaurants in the catalogue. | S-001, S-010 | T-003, T-026 |
| R-012 | non_functional (security) | must | Card data never reaches the platform's servers; passwords are stored only as salted hashes; all traffic uses HTTPS. | S-003, S-004 | T-009, T-011, T-012, T-013 |
| R-013 | non_functional (reliability) | must | Ordering is available 99.5% of each month, and an accepted order is never lost when a service restarts. | S-005, S-010 | T-014, T-023, T-024, T-025, T-027 |

## Epics, stories and tasks

### E-001 Customer Ordering

Everything a customer does before paying: finding a restaurant, building a cart, placing an order and keeping an account.

#### S-001 Search and browse nearby restaurants by cuisine, name or dish

Priority: must. Requirements: R-001, R-011. 16 points in 4 tasks.

As a hungry customer, I want to search and browse nearby restaurants by cuisine, name or dish, so that I can quickly find something I want to eat.

Acceptance criteria:

- The restaurant list shows only restaurants that deliver to the customer's location, sorted by distance by default.
- Customers can filter by cuisine and search by restaurant or dish name.
- A menu shows each item with a photo, price and description; unavailable items are greyed out and cannot be added.
- Search and menu pages respond in under 2 seconds at the 95th percentile.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-001 | Wireframes and design system for the ordering flow | design | 3 | 12 | 1 | - |
| T-002 (critical) | Restaurant and menu database schema | database | 3 | 12 | 1 | - |
| T-003 (critical) | Restaurant search and menu API | backend | 5 | 20 | 1 | T-002 |
| T-004 | Restaurant list and menu screens | frontend | 5 | 20 | 3 | T-001, T-003 |

#### S-002 Add dishes to a cart and place an order for my delivery address

Priority: must. Requirements: R-002. 13 points in 3 tasks.

As a customer, I want to add dishes to a cart and place an order for my delivery address, so that the food is prepared and brought to my door.

Acceptance criteria:

- A cart holds items from one restaurant only; adding an item from another restaurant asks the customer to start a new cart.
- The cart shows item totals, the delivery fee and the order total, and updates them as quantities change.
- Checkout requires a delivery address and accepts an optional note to the restaurant.
- If an item becomes unavailable or its price changes, the customer is told before the order is placed.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-005 | Order and order-item schema | database | 3 | 12 | 1 | T-002 |
| T-006 (critical) | Cart and order placement API | backend | 5 | 20 | 1 | T-003, T-005, T-009 |
| T-007 | Cart and checkout screens | frontend | 5 | 20 | 2 | T-001, T-006 |

#### S-003 Register and sign in with my email and password

Priority: must. Requirements: R-003, R-012. 10 points in 3 tasks.

As a new user, I want to register and sign in with my email and password, so that my addresses and order history are saved.

Acceptance criteria:

- A user can register with an email address and a password of at least 10 characters.
- Passwords are stored only as salted hashes and sessions expire after 30 days of inactivity.
- Signed-in customers can save, edit and delete delivery addresses and view past orders.
- Restaurant staff and couriers sign in through the same service and only see their own tools.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-008 | User, role and address schema | database | 2 | 8 | 1 | - |
| T-009 | Authentication and session API | backend | 5 | 20 | 1 | T-008 |
| T-010 | Sign-up, sign-in and address book screens | frontend | 3 | 12 | 2 | T-009 |

### E-002 Payments and Live Tracking

Taking the payment securely, moving the order through its states and keeping the customer informed until delivery.

#### S-004 Pay for my order by card or digital wallet

Priority: must. Requirements: R-004, R-012. 16 points in 3 tasks.

As a customer, I want to pay for my order by card or digital wallet, so that my order is confirmed without handling cash.

Acceptance criteria:

- Card details are entered in the payment provider's hosted fields and never reach our servers.
- An order is sent to the restaurant only after the provider confirms the payment.
- A declined payment shows a clear message and keeps the cart so the customer can retry.
- A payment confirmation is shown on screen and sent by email, and duplicate webhooks never charge or confirm twice.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-011 | Integrate payment provider (hosted fields and webhooks) | integration | 8 | 32 | 1 | - |
| T-012 (critical) | Payment and order confirmation flow | backend | 5 | 20 | 2 | T-006, T-011 |
| T-013 | Payment form and confirmation screen | frontend | 3 | 12 | 2 | T-007, T-012 |

#### S-005 Watch my order progress and see the courier on a map

Priority: must. Requirements: R-005, R-013. 15 points in 3 tasks.

As a customer, I want to watch my order progress and see the courier on a map, so that I know when to expect my food.

Acceptance criteria:

- The order page shows the current status: placed, accepted, preparing, picked up, delivered or cancelled.
- While the order is on the way, the courier's position on the map refreshes at least every 10 seconds.
- The page updates without a manual refresh and recovers after a dropped connection.
- An accepted order and its status history are stored durably and survive a service restart.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-014 (critical) | Order status state machine and live update stream | backend | 5 | 20 | 2 | T-012 |
| T-015 | Map tiles and courier location ingestion | integration | 5 | 20 | 1 | - |
| T-016 | Live order tracking page with map | frontend | 5 | 20 | 2 | T-014, T-015 |

#### S-006 Be notified when my order changes status

Priority: should. Requirements: R-006. 3 points in 1 tasks.

As a customer, I want to be notified when my order changes status, so that I do not have to keep the app open.

Acceptance criteria:

- A notification is sent when the order is accepted, picked up and delivered.
- Customers can choose push, SMS or email, and can switch notifications off.
- A failed notification is retried and never blocks the order from moving forward.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-017 | Notification gateway for push, SMS and email | integration | 3 | 12 | 2 | T-014 |

### E-003 Restaurant and Courier Operations

The tools restaurant staff and couriers use to run their side of an order.

#### S-007 Edit my menu, prices and item availability

Priority: must. Requirements: R-003, R-007. 8 points in 2 tasks.

As a restaurant manager, I want to edit my menu, prices and item availability, so that customers always see what I can really serve.

Acceptance criteria:

- A manager can add, edit and delete menu items with name, description, photo and price.
- An item can be switched to unavailable with one action and is immediately greyed out for customers.
- Menu changes are visible to customers within one minute.
- Only staff of that restaurant can change its menu.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-018 | Restaurant menu management API | backend | 3 | 12 | 2 | T-002, T-009 |
| T-019 | Restaurant dashboard: menu editor | frontend | 5 | 20 | 3 | T-018 |

#### S-008 See new orders and accept or reject them with a preparation time

Priority: must. Requirements: R-008. 5 points in 1 tasks.

As a restaurant staff member, I want to see new orders and accept or reject them with a preparation time, so that I stay in control of the kitchen's workload.

Acceptance criteria:

- A new paid order appears in the inbox within 5 seconds and plays a sound until it is answered.
- Staff can accept an order with a preparation time, or reject it with a reason.
- An order that is not answered within 3 minutes is cancelled and the customer is refunded.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-020 | Restaurant order inbox with accept and reject | frontend | 5 | 20 | 2 | T-014 |

#### S-009 Receive delivery offers, accept one and update its status

Priority: must. Requirements: R-009. 13 points in 2 tasks.

As a courier, I want to receive delivery offers, accept one and update its status, so that I can pick up and deliver orders efficiently.

Acceptance criteria:

- When an order is accepted, nearby available couriers receive an offer showing pickup, drop-off and earnings.
- The first courier to accept gets the job; the others see it disappear.
- The courier marks the order picked up and delivered, and the app shares the courier's position while the job is active.
- If no courier accepts within 5 minutes, operations staff are alerted.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-021 (critical) | Courier matching and dispatch service | backend | 8 | 32 | 3 | T-014 |
| T-022 (critical) | Courier web app: offers, jobs and status updates | frontend | 5 | 20 | 3 | T-015, T-021 |

### E-004 Platform and Reliability

Build pipeline, monitoring, performance and end-to-end verification so the service can launch and stay up.

#### S-010 Automated deployment, monitoring and load testing

Priority: must. Requirements: R-011, R-013. 18 points in 5 tasks.

As a platform operator, I want automated deployment, monitoring and load testing, so that ordering stays fast and available as traffic grows.

Acceptance criteria:

- Every merge to the main branch is built, tested and deployed to a staging environment automatically.
- Error rate, latency and queue depth are visible on a dashboard, and an alert fires when ordering fails for 5 minutes.
- A load test of search and checkout confirms the 2-second p95 target before release.
- An end-to-end test covers the full order journey from sign-in to delivery.

| Task | Title | Layer | Points | Hours | Sprint | Depends on |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| T-023 | CI/CD pipeline and staging environment | devops | 5 | 20 | 3 | - |
| T-024 | Monitoring, logging and alerting | devops | 3 | 12 | 3 | T-023 |
| T-025 (critical) | End-to-end order journey tests | testing | 5 | 20 | 4 | T-013, T-016, T-020, T-022, T-023 |
| T-026 | Load test of search and checkout | testing | 3 | 12 | 2 | T-003, T-006 |
| T-027 (critical) | Production release and rollback runbook | devops | 2 | 8 | 4 | T-024, T-025, T-026 |

